Hello, 

I am trying to get UART2 running on the ESP32 (In particular, the Huzzah board- ESP WROOM). I've left the esp32 dtsi file as configured, including the section with disables uart0, uart1, uart2 through `status = "disabled"; `. The relevant section of the devicetree (dts) for the ESP32 is as follows:


```
&uart0 {
        status = "okay";
        current-speed = <115200>;
        tx-pin = <1>;
        rx-pin = <3>;
        rts-pin = <22>;
        cts-pin = <19>;
};

&uart1 {
        status = "okay";
        current-speed = <115200>;
        tx-pin = <10>;
        rx-pin = <9>;
        rts-pin = <11>;
        cts-pin = <6>;
        hw-flow-control;
};

&uart2 {
        status = "okay";
        current-speed = <115200>;
        tx-pin = <17>;
        rx-pin = <16>;
        rts-pin = <7>;
        cts-pin = <8>;
        hw-flow-control;
};
```

The only change from default is adding  status = "okay". When I compile and run any code with this setting, even "Hello World", I do not see program output on the terminal after the program has been booted. Why is this? Enabling UART1 and UART2 should not cause any changes in default operation.
